  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the maximum magnitude outcome and its probability — is not considered by the individual. The individual only considers the probability of winning (i.e., getting a positive payout), not the magnitude of the payout or a weighted comparison of the maximum outcomes. The decision reason requires evaluating the maximum outcome (2500 vs. 2400) and weighting it by its probability (33% vs. 34%), which was not part of the individual's reasoning. Instead, the individual’s justification is based on a simple comparison of the probability of winning, which is a different criterion. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not apply the rule of weighting the maximum magnitude outcome by its probability, nor did they reference the magnitude of the outcomes. The reasoning is distinct from the decision reason provided.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
